    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="1094" n="962" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg962"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4976: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-04T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                                1926—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 4—1:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>528. Your 254, October 30, 11 p.m. There would appear to be good ground for
                    believing that such plans are under way with probability that P’an Fu<anchor
                        n="40" xml:id="d740-f1"/> has gained support of Chang Tso-lin<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d740-f2"/> and Chang Tsung-chang<anchor n="42" xml:id="d740-f3"/> by
                    promise of 3,000,000 to each. I am keeping close watch on the matter and shall
                    avail myself of Department’s authorization to protest if the occasion
                    warrants.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d740-f1" n="40" xml:id="d740-f1-content">
